<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore suspends pork imports from Taiwan.</title>
<headline>Singapore suspends pork imports from Taiwan.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore has suspended pork imports from Taiwan due to the outbreak of foot-and-mouth disease there, state television said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Singapore imported only a small amount of pork from Taiwan, it said. No further details were immediately available.</p>
<p>The disease has crippled Taiwan's multi-billion dollar pork industry. Japan, which takes most of Taiwan's pork exports, and South Korea have indefinitely suspended the import of pork products from Taiwan.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65-8703305)</p>
</text>
